\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Two labeled products on a common target}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{Y_1:F_1\to E} and #{Y_2:F_2\to E} be complex-linear
maps between finite-dimensional Hermitian spaces. Their
\newvocab{ordered Gram pair} on the common target #{E} is
##{(A,B)=(Y_1Y_1^\dagger,Y_2Y_2^\dagger).}
The first and second positions retain the channel labels.
Adjoints use the supplied inner products.}

\p{For a finite word #{w} in two letters, #{w(A,B)} is the
ordered product obtained by substituting #{A} for the first
letter and #{B} for the second. The empty word gives
#{\bbI_E}. The corresponding trace is #{\trace(w(A,B))}.}
